# SereneDB compiles extensions into the server binary. LOAD / INSTALL of an
# extension that is already compiled in has nothing to do, so it succeeds
# silently and the usual DuckDB `INSTALL x; LOAD x;` preamble just works.
# Anything not compiled in cannot be provided at runtime and must surface a
# clear SereneDB error pointing at the SereneDB issue tracker -- never a
# duckdb.org link, a local extension path, or a network download attempt
# (see https://github.com/serenedb/serenedb/issues/768).


statement ok
LOAD inet;


statement ok
INSTALL inet;


statement ok
FORCE INSTALL inet;


statement ok
INSTALL httpfs FROM community;


statement error
LOAD 'spatial';
----
db error: ERROR: LOAD is not supported by SereneDB: extensions are compiled into the server binary and cannot be loaded at runtime.
If you need the "spatial" extension, please open an issue at https://github.com/serenedb/serenedb/issues/887.


statement error
INSTALL sqlite_scanner;
----
db error: ERROR: INSTALL is not supported by SereneDB: extensions are compiled into the server binary and cannot be installed at runtime.
If you need the "sqlite_scanner" extension, please open an issue at https://github.com/serenedb/serenedb/issues/887.


statement error
UPDATE EXTENSIONS;
----
db error: ERROR: UPDATE EXTENSIONS is not supported by SereneDB: extensions are compiled into the server binary and cannot be updated at runtime.
If you are missing an extension, please open an issue at https://github.com/serenedb/serenedb/issues/887.
